mytests.exe - windtrap test runner

usage: mytests.exe [OPTIONS] [PATTERN]

A bare PATTERN runs only tests whose full path contains it (same as
-f PATTERN). Under `dune runtest`, set options through their
WINDTRAP_* environment mirrors instead.

OPTIONS:
  -f, --filter PATTERN          Run only tests whose path contains PATTERN
  -e, --exclude PATTERN         Skip tests whose path contains PATTERN
      --tag LABEL               Run only tests tagged LABEL (repeatable)
      --exclude-tag LABEL       Skip tests tagged LABEL (repeatable)
      --shard K/N               Run only the Kth of N deterministic path-hash buckets
      --failed                  Rerun only the last run's failures
  -l, --list                    List selected tests without running them
  -x, --fail-fast               Stop after the first failure (same as --bail 1)
      --bail N                  Stop after N failures
      --timeout SECONDS         Default per-test timeout in seconds
      --slow-threshold SECONDS  Warn when an untagged test runs longer than SECONDS (0 disables)
      --seed TOKEN              Root seed for property tests (s1:<16 hex>)
      --prop-count N            Generated cases per property
      --max-shrink N            Accepted shrink steps per failing property
  -u, --update                  Accept snapshot changes (refused under CI)
  -s, --stream                  Stream test output instead of capturing it
  -v, --verbose                 One status line per test
      --junit PATH              Also write a JUnit XML report to PATH
      --color MODE              Color output: always, never or auto
  -o, --output DIR              Root directory for capture logs
  -V, --version                 Print the version and exit
  -h, --help                    Print this help and exit

ENVIRONMENT:
  WINDTRAP_FILTER          Mirror of --filter
  WINDTRAP_EXCLUDE         Mirror of --exclude
  WINDTRAP_TAG             Mirror of --tag
  WINDTRAP_EXCLUDE_TAG     Mirror of --exclude-tag
  WINDTRAP_SHARD           Mirror of --shard
  WINDTRAP_BAIL            Mirror of --bail
  WINDTRAP_TIMEOUT         Mirror of --timeout
  WINDTRAP_SLOW_THRESHOLD  Mirror of --slow-threshold
  WINDTRAP_SEED            Mirror of --seed
  WINDTRAP_PROP_COUNT      Mirror of --prop-count
  WINDTRAP_MAX_SHRINK      Mirror of --max-shrink
  WINDTRAP_UPDATE          Mirror of --update
  WINDTRAP_STREAM          Mirror of --stream
  WINDTRAP_VERBOSE         Mirror of --verbose
  WINDTRAP_JUNIT           Mirror of --junit
  WINDTRAP_COLOR           Mirror of --color
  WINDTRAP_OUTPUT          Mirror of --output
  WINDTRAP_TAIL_ERRORS     Captured-output lines shown per failure
  WINDTRAP_PROJECT_ROOT    Project root for snapshot path resolution
  WINDTRAP_COVERAGE        Inline coverage line: on or off
  WINDTRAP_COVERAGE_ONLY   Source prefixes the coverage number covers
  WINDTRAP_MUTATE          Mutation testing: 1, admit or off
  WINDTRAP_MUTATE_ARM      Arm one mutant, by identifier
  WINDTRAP_MUTATE_TRY      Faults an admit run tries per test (0 for all)
  WINDTRAP_MUTATE_ONLY     Source prefixes whose mutants a run considers
  NO_COLOR                 Any value: never style output (--color auto)
